<Project>
  <!-- ==================================================================================================================
       Imported by every Gym.NET project (src/, tests/, examples/). refs/NumSharp keeps its own Directory.Build.props, which
       MSBuild finds first for NumSharp's projects, so nothing here reaches them.

       NuGet audit suppressions for SixLabors.ImageSharp 2.1.13 (decision D18, docs/plans/COMPLETION_PLAN.md step R0.2).

       2.1.13 is the last ImageSharp release under Apache-2.0; every later version ships under the Six Labors Split
       License, whose build check fails Release builds and packs without a license key (measured 2026-09-23). On
       2026-10-07 GitHub published five advisories against 2.1.13, fixed only in 3.2.0 and 4.1.2. NuGet audit reports
       them as NU1902/NU1903, and the projects that set TreatWarningsAsErrors (Gym.Rendering, Gym.Tests.Parity) then fail
       restore. The maintainer chose to suppress them and keep 2.1.13.

       Why none of them applies to Gym.NET: Gym.NET builds images from pixel buffers for the human viewers and the legacy
       Render(), writes PNG artifacts in the parity suite and the RecordVideo wrapper's frame folders, and decodes
       only the PNG assets copied from Gymnasium (step P7.4). It never encodes TIFF, never reads BigTIFF, never runs
       HistogramEqualization, and never decodes an untrusted image, which is the only way to reach the ICC-profile parser.

       Scope: these suppressions quiet Gym.NET's own build only. A consumer of the Gym.NET packages still restores 2.1.13
       and gets the same advisories in their own build; the release notes say so (P10.4). A new advisory against 2.1.13 is
       NOT suppressed here: it fails the build again on purpose, and gets the same review before a line is added below.
       ================================================================================================================== -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- High: "HistogramEqualization uses an unvalidated luminance as an unchecked histogram index". Gym.NET never applies
         histogram equalization. -->
    <NuGetAuditSuppress Include="https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-j3p4-wp97-rph4" />
    <!-- High: "TIFF CCITT T4 encoder can write past its compressed output buffer". Gym.NET never encodes TIFF. -->
    <NuGetAuditSuppress Include="https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-j9gm-c75j-xc9q" />
    <!-- High: "TIFF CCITT T6 encoder writes beyond an undersized output buffer". Gym.NET never encodes TIFF. -->
    <NuGetAuditSuppress Include="https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-jjfr-hcj7-qf5w" />
    <!-- Moderate: "ICC CLUT parsing allocates from unvalidated channel and grid dimensions". Reached only by decoding an
         image with an embedded ICC profile; Gym.NET decodes only Gymnasium's own PNG assets, never untrusted input. -->
    <NuGetAuditSuppress Include="https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-gwg2-r3hj-4w44" />
    <!-- Moderate: "BigTIFF IFD count can keep a decoder thread in a non-progressing loop". Gym.NET never decodes TIFF. -->
    <NuGetAuditSuppress Include="https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-wmxv-xphr-5c9g" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
